ALMA iOS Agent Voice / CallKit Handoff
=====================================

Branch
------
codex/ios-voice-callkit-handoff

Purpose
-------
This branch contains only the iOS Agent voice/CallKit reliability fix and its
regression coverage. It intentionally excludes the unrelated Agent Chat work
that was concurrently present in the original main worktree.

What was broken
---------------
1. Gemini websocket setupComplete and CallKit didActivate could arrive in either
   order. The app published LIVE and started the timer before CallKit actually
   owned active audio hardware, producing an answered but silent call. Opening
   the app or toggling speaker happened to recover the graph later.
2. AVAudioSession used defaultToSpeaker. Clearing a temporary speaker override
   with .none therefore still selected the speaker, so speaker OFF could not
   reliably select the receiver/earpiece.
3. CallKit didDeactivate, provider reset, and system mute were not fully routed
   to the Agent voice engine.
4. Foreground recovery could self-activate a CallKit-owned audio session and
   race CallKit. Route state reflected the requested button state rather than
   the actual hardware route.

What this branch changes
------------------------
- Adds AlmaLiveAudioReadiness, a lock-protected two-signal gate. A CallKit call
  becomes LIVE only after socket setup, audio configuration, CallKit activation,
  and a successful audio graph start/restart.
- Handles both activation orderings, deactivation/reactivation, and websocket
  reconnect generations without reusing stale readiness.
- Treats audio graph restart failure as a bounded retry instead of publishing a
  silent LIVE timer.
- Removes defaultToSpeaker and explicitly routes .speaker / .none, allowing
  .none to resolve to the receiver when no Bluetooth/wired route is active.
- Publishes the actual AVAudioSession route back to UI and enables proximity
  monitoring only for the built-in receiver.
- Propagates CallKit didDeactivate, mute, and provider reset to agent calls.
- Prevents foreground recovery from self-activating CallKit-owned audio.

Scoped files
------------
- ios/App/App/AssistantVoiceSwiftUI.swift
- ios/App/App/AgentCallUI.swift
- ios/App/App/CallKitVoIP.swift
- ios/App/AppParityV2Tests/AssistantParityV2Tests.swift
- src/agent/lib/__tests__/native-voice-upload-contract.test.ts

Integration instructions for the Agent Chat session
---------------------------------------------------
1. Preserve/commit the Agent Chat session's own work first.
2. Merge this branch, or cherry-pick its single scoped commit.
3. If AssistantParityV2Tests.swift conflicts, keep BOTH the Agent Chat tests and
   the three testLiveAudioGate... methods from this branch. Do not accept either
   whole-file side.
4. If any production voice file conflicts, preserve these invariants:
   - no LIVE before socketSetupComplete + audioConfigured + CallKit audio active;
   - no defaultToSpeaker in AlmaGeminiLiveSession live configuration;
   - speaker OFF calls overrideOutputAudioPort(.none);
   - didDeactivate reaches AgentCallController.audioSessionDeactivated();
   - CallKit-owned recoverAudio never calls setActive(true) while inactive.
5. Run the combined Agent Chat tests as well as every verification below.

Important test-target integration dependency
--------------------------------------------
Clean main at 06624dfa has the AppParityV2Tests target, but that target does not
inherit the CocoaPods framework/module search paths needed to import the App
module (AgoraRtcKit, Capacitor, OneSignal, and related dependencies). The active
Agent Chat worktree already contains pending project.pbxproj + Podfile test-target
wiring; that is why the combined worktree can run the suite. This handoff branch
deliberately does NOT duplicate those files, because doing so would create the
exact conflict this branch is designed to avoid.

Therefore, retain the Agent Chat session's project/Podfile test wiring during the
merge, run pod install, and then run the full suite. If the combined suite cannot
resolve those modules, the merge dropped that test wiring; do not work around it
by deleting the voice tests.

Required simulator verification
-------------------------------
Use the dedicated simulator, not the Pro Max used by another session:

  Device: Alma Voice Verify iPhone 17 Pro
  Model:  iPhone 17 Pro
  OS:     iOS 26.5
  UDID:   83770047-A463-4F0F-8DB6-F9DA1191B3B4

Commands (adjust DerivedData path if needed):

  npm test -- --run src/agent/lib/__tests__/native-voice-upload-contract.test.ts

  cd ios/App
  xcodebuild -workspace App.xcworkspace -scheme App -configuration Debug \
    -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,id=83770047-A463-4F0F-8DB6-F9DA1191B3B4' \
    -derivedDataPath /tmp/alma-voice-handoff-derived \
    -only-testing:AppParityV2Tests/AssistantParityV2Tests \
    CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO test

  xcodebuild -workspace App.xcworkspace -scheme App -configuration Debug \
    -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' \
    -derivedDataPath /tmp/alma-voice-handoff-device-derived \
    CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build

Prior verification evidence
---------------------------
- Dedicated fresh iPhone 17 Pro simulator boot/install/launch: passed.
- AssistantParityV2Tests: 26/26 passed on that simulator in the active combined
  worktree containing the same five voice changes plus Agent Chat test wiring.
- Native voice contract Vitest file: 7/7 passed.
- Isolated handoff branch Simulator Debug app build: passed.
- Generic physical-iPhone arm64 build, including the non-simulator voice
  processing branch: passed.
- git diff --check: passed.

Standalone clean-main note: attempting the test action before Agent Chat's test
wiring is merged reaches and successfully builds the App target, then stops only
at AppParityV2Tests module resolution. This is a base test-infrastructure issue,
not a production voice compile error. The combined branch MUST still achieve a
green full suite before requesting TestFlight approval.

Hard verification before TestFlight
-----------------------------------
Simulator cannot reproduce PushKit delivery, genuine CallKit activation,
built-in receiver acoustics, or proximity behavior. After merging the Agent Chat
work, a signed build must be tested on a real iPhone with these cases:

[ ] Cold-launch Agent 2-way voice: first attempt speaks without exiting/retrying.
[ ] In-app voice after app relaunch: first greeting is audible.
[ ] Incoming agent call answered while app foregrounded: immediate audible speech.
[ ] Incoming agent call answered while app backgrounded: immediate audible speech.
[ ] Incoming agent call answered from locked screen: immediate audible speech.
[ ] Speaker ON: loud built-in speaker and UI reports speaker route.
[ ] Speaker OFF: built-in receiver/earpiece, lower private-call volume.
[ ] Receiver route: proximity sensor blanks/restores screen near/far from ear.
[ ] CallKit/system mute: microphone actually mutes and unmutes.
[ ] Audio interruption/deactivate/reactivate: speech resumes without opening app
    or manually toggling speaker.
[ ] Network reconnect during a call: conversation resumes without a stale LIVE
    state or permanently silent audio.
[ ] End/reset: no orphan timer, audio graph, proximity state, or active call UI.

TestFlight approval gate
------------------------
DO NOT archive, upload, submit, or distribute a TestFlight build automatically.
After the combined branch passes the simulator suite, generic device build, and
the merge-conflict invariant review, report the exact results and ask the owner:

  "Agent Chat + Agent voice fixes একসাথে hard-verified। এখন কি TestFlight
   archive/upload শুরু করব?"

Proceed only after an explicit YES. If approved, create one combined TestFlight
build from the Agent Chat session's final integration branch; do not publish a
separate build from this handoff branch.

Known boundary
--------------
The fresh simulator had no authenticated owner session, and simulator hardware
cannot prove true CallKit/receiver behavior. The source-level race, routing,
lifecycle, regression, simulator, and arm64 compilation gates are complete; the
real-iPhone checklist above is the final acceptance gate.
